          "content": "{\n  \"contentId\": \"test-ai-healthcare\",\n  \"hooks\": [\n    {\n      \"text\": \"What if the future of medicine isn't about better doctors, but about better algorithms working alongside them?\",\n      \"type\": \"question\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"In the time it takes a radiologist to drink a cup of coffee, an AI can analyze hundreds of medical images with 95% accuracy.\",\n      \"type\": \"story\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"60% of healthcare systems are now racing to implement AI—but 90% of patients have no idea it's already happening.\",\n      \"type\": \"statistic\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"Everyone's worried about AI replacing doctors. The real story is more surprising: AI might actually save the profession.\",\n      \"type\": \"curiosity\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"For decades, we've accepted that drug development takes 15 years. What if that timeline isn't a law of nature, but just an engineering problem?\",\n      \"type\": \"bold-statement\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"angles\": [\n    {\n      \"perspective\": \"The Skeptic's Audit\",\n      \"approach\": \"Examine each AI healthcare claim through a critical lens—what's real, what's hype, and what are the hidden dangers of algorithmic bias in medicine?\",\n      \"target\": \"Readers who question tech optimism and want balanced analysis\",\n      \"relevanceScore\": 0.8\n    },\n    {\n      \"perspective\": \"Patient's Eye View\",\n      \"approach\": \"Walk through what AI in healthcare actually looks like from the patient perspective—getting a diagnosis, choosing treatment, navigating privacy concerns.\",\n      \"target\": \"General readers wondering how this affects their own healthcare experience\",\n      \"relevanceScore\": 0.9\n    },\n    {\n      \"perspective\": \"Doctor in the Machine\",\n      \"approach\": \"Profile the changing role of physicians—from diagnosticians to AI supervisors, interpreters, and patient advocates. How medical training must evolve.\",\n      \"target\": \"Healthcare professionals, medical students, and those interested in career futures\",\n      \"relevanceScore\": 0.85\n    },\n    {\n      \"perspective\": \"The Race to the Cure\",\n      \"approach\": \"Deep dive into drug discovery acceleration—specific case studies of AI-identified compounds, timeline comparisons, and what this means for diseases with no current treatment.\",\n      \"target\": \"Patients, researchers, and anyone following specific disease research\",\n      \"relevanceScore\": 0.75\n    },\n    {\n      \"perspective\": \"Implementation Reality Check\",\n      \"approach\": \"Beyond the hype—what's actually happening on the ground? Hospital IT integration challenges, regulatory hurdles, and why adoption is harder than it looks.\",\n      \"target\": \"Healthcare administrators, policymakers, and implementation specialists\",\n      \"relevanceScore\": 0.7\n    }\n  ],\n  \"questions\": [\n    {\n      \"text\": \"How would you feel about an AI diagnosing your condition? Would you trust it more or less than a human doctor?\",\n      \"type\": \"personal\",\n      \"depth\": \"medium\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"If AI can detect cancer earlier than human radiologists, is it ethical for healthcare systems NOT to use it?\",\n      \"type\": \"ethical\",\n      \"depth\": \"deep\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"What happens to the doctor-patient relationship when diagnosis becomes automated? Is something valuable lost?\",\n      \"type\": \"philosophical\",\n      \"depth\": \"deep\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"If personalized medicine based on your genome becomes standard, who owns that genetic data? Your insurance company? Your employer?\",\n      \"type\": \"practical\",\n      \"depth\": \"medium\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"Should AI medical systems be required to explain their reasoning, or is accuracy alone sufficient?\",\n      \"type\": \"analytical\",\n      \"depth\": \"deep\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"How do we ensure AI doesn't inherit and amplify existing healthcare disparities in training data?\",\n      \"type\": \"comparative\",\n      \"depth\": \"deep\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"If AI reduces drug development from 15 years to 5, should those savings be passed to patients or captured by pharmaceutical companies?\",\n      \"type\": \"practical\",\n      \"depth\": \"medium\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"personalization\": {\n    \"matchedTopics\": [],\n    \"adjustedFor\": \"intermediate expertise\",\n    \"tone\": \"first-person\",\n    \"targetWordCount\": 1000,\n    \"relevanceScore\": 0.5\n  },\n  \"expandedAngles\": [\n    {\n      \"angle\": \"The Hidden Cost Question\",\n      \"development\": \"AI diagnostics might be cheaper and faster—but what about the upfront costs? The infrastructure, training, and implementation budgets that smaller hospitals can't afford. Does this create a two-tier healthcare system where only wealthy institutions get AI capabilities?\",\n      \"opening\": \"The revolution is here, but can everyone afford to join it?\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"angle\": \" Liability Loophole\",\n      \"development\": \"When an AI misses a diagnosis, who's responsible? The doctor who trusted the system? The hospital that bought it? The company that built it? We're building a legal gray area into the foundation of future medicine.\",\n      \"opening\": \"We know who's to blame when a doctor makes a mistake. But what happens when the doctor is an algorithm?\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"angle\": \"The Data Feedback Loop\",\n      \"development\": \"AI systems need data to improve. But they need diverse, high-quality data. What happens when most early data comes from wealthy, urban, predominantly white patient populations? The AI gets better at serving some patients while remaining inadequate for others.\",\n      \"opening\": \"The better AI gets at medicine, the worse it might get at equity.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n"
