          "content": "{\n  \"contentId\": \"test-ai-healthcare\",\n  \"source\": {\n    \"type\": \"article\",\n    \"title\": \"The Future of AI in Healthcare\",\n    \"url\": \"https://example.com/ai-healthcare\",\n    \"publishedAt\": \"2024-12-08T00:00:00Z\"\n  },\n  \"summary\": {\n    \"headline\": \"AI is transforming healthcare through faster diagnostics, accelerated drug discovery, and personalized medicine\",\n    \"tldr\": \"Artificial intelligence is fundamentally transforming healthcare across three major domains: diagnostic imaging (achieving 95%+ accuracy in cancer detection), drug discovery (dramatically reducing traditional 10-15 year timelines), and personalized medicine (analyzing genetic and lifestyle data to predict disease risk). Rather than replacing medical professionals, AI will augment them by handling routine tasks while humans focus on complex cases and treatment planning.\",\n    \"bullets\": [\n      \"AI-powered imaging can detect certain cancers earlier than human radiologists with 95%+ accuracy\",\n      \"AI processes medical images in seconds versus 15 minutes for human radiologists\",\n      \"Drug development time of 10-15 years is being significantly reduced through AI screening of molecular compounds\",\n      \"Personalized medicine analyzes genetic data, medical history, and lifestyle to predict disease risk and select effective treatments\",\n      \"60% of healthcare systems are now exploring or implementing AI solutions, up from 30% three years ago\",\n      \"Key challenges include data privacy, training data bias, regulatory uncertainty, and system integration\",\n      \"AI will augment rather than replace medical professionals by handling routine tasks and flagging unusual cases\"\n    ],\n    \"keyThemes\": [\n      \"Diagnostic Transformation\",\n      \"Drug Discovery Acceleration\",\n      \"Personalized Medicine\",\n      \"Human-AI Collaboration\",\n      \"Implementation Challenges\"\n    ],\n    \"importantQuotes\": [\n      {\n        \"text\": \"Artificial intelligence is fundamentally transforming the healthcare industry. From diagnostic imaging to personalized medicine, AI systems are becoming integral to modern medical practice.\",\n        \"context\": \"Opening statement establishing the scope and significance of AI's impact on healthcare\",\n        \"significance\": \"Sets the tone - positions this as fundamental transformation, not incremental change\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"text\": \"Machine learning models trained on millions of medical images have achieved accuracy rates exceeding 95% in detecting breast cancer, lung cancer, and other conditions.\",\n        \"context\": \"Specific evidence supporting AI diagnostic capabilities\",\n        \"significance\": \"Concrete data point demonstrating AI's superiority in specific diagnostic tasks\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"text\": \"What might take a radiologist 15 minutes to analyze, an AI system can process in seconds, allowing radiologists to focus on complex cases and treatment planning rather than routine image analysis.\",\n        \"context\": \"Explaining the practical advantage of AI speed in diagnostic workflows\",\n        \"significance\": \"Highlights how AI changes the radiologist's role to higher-value work\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"text\": \"Traditionally, developing a new drug takes 10-15 years and costs billions. AI is accelerating this process significantly.\",\n        \"context\": \"Establishing the scale of improvement in drug discovery\",\n        \"significance\": \"Frames the traditional drug development timeline as the problem AI solves\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"text\": \"AI enables truly personalized medicine by analyzing a patient's genetic data, medical history, lifestyle factors, and molecular markers.\",\n        \"context\": \"Defining personalized medicine in the AI context\",\n        \"significance\": \"Shows how AI makes theoretical personalization practically possible at scale\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"text\": \"Rather than replacing doctors, AI will augment medical professionals by handling routine diagnostic tasks, flagging unusual cases for specialist review, suggesting treatment options based on latest research, and monitoring patient outcomes to improve care.\",\n        \"context\": \"The article's conclusion about the future relationship between AI and doctors\",\n        \"significance\": \"Key takeaway - positions AI as augmentation tool rather than replacement\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"text\": \"According to recent surveys, 60% of healthcare systems are exploring or implementing AI solutions, up from 30% just three years ago.\",\n        \"context\": \"Evidence of accelerating adoption in healthcare\",\n        \"significance\": \"Demonstrates this is not speculative - real adoption is happening rapidly\"\n      }\n    ]\n  },\n  \"ideas\": {\n    \"hooks\": [\n      {\n        \"text\": \"What if the future of medicine isn't about better doctors, but about better algorithms working alongside them?\",\n        \"type\": \"question\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"text\": \"In the time it takes a radiologist to drink a cup of coffee, an AI can analyze hundreds of medical images with 95% accuracy.\",\n        \"type\": \"story\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"text\": \"60% of healthcare systems are now racing to implement AI—but 90% of patients have no idea it's already happening.\",\n        \"type\": \"statistic\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"text\": \"Everyone's worried about AI replacing doctors. The real story is more surprising: AI might actually save the profession.\",\n        \"type\": \"curiosity\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"text\": \"For decades, we've accepted that drug development takes 15 years. What if that timeline isn't a law of nature, but just an engineering problem?\",\n        \"type\": \"bold-statement\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"angles\": [\n      {\n        \"perspective\": \